# The WinAPI surface the TeaVM port of jr binds. THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH: WinApi.java and
# WinOffsets.java are generated from it by gen-bindings.cmd - never hand-edit them.
# One C name per line, optionally followed by the Java name. Functions, constants (#define, enum)
# and struct names all go here; the tool asks clang what each one is. `struct:<tag>` for a struct
# tag shadowed by an ordinary name. Anything the tool cannot bind is reported NOT BOUND (exit 1).
# `escapes=N[,M]` after a function's Java name: the C function keeps parameter N (1-based) after it
# returns, which no header says (PRP-35 phase 4); it becomes @Escapes, and never a String overload.
# `releases=a[,b]` after a function's Java name: the Java names of the calls that close what it returns (PRP-35
# phase 5); it becomes @Acquires("a,b") and teavm-native-check NC8 checks every caller closes it on every path.
# Not covered: resources returned through an out-parameter (CreateProcessW, BCryptOpenAlgorithmProvider), child
# windows (their parent destroys them), CertEnumCertificatesInStore (each call frees the previous context).
# `fails=V` after a function's Java name: the value it returns on failure (NULL, or a constant such as
# INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE); it becomes @Fails("V") and NC10 makes every caller test the result against V before using
# it (PRP-35 phase 8). Left out: GetStdHandle (fails with either), GetConsoleWindow (NULL is "no console", a state).
# --- functions (C name, Java name) ---
